<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeCreateFromError</function></refname>
  <refpurpose></refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoNode *SilikoNodeCreateFromError(enum SilikoError source);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The `SilikoSyntaxTreeNewError` function creates new
`SilikoSyntaxTreeNode` object representing a syntax error.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para>`SilikoSyntaxTreeNewError` returns a pointer to a
new error `SilikoSyntaxTreeNode` object on success, or `NULL` if there
was a memory error.</para>
</refsection>
